// 289's anvil smithing (skill_smithing/scripts/smithing/smithing.rs2) on 2011's
// anvil interface, smithing_new (300, cache 786). 289 transmitted the products
// in inv columns (smithing.inv) and its interface coloured their names and bars
// itself from %modified_smith and %smithbars. 2011's has a slot per product,
// with Make All, X, 5 and 1 under it, and no script to fill them (its one
// onload, cs2 870, places its scrollbar): the server
// puts each product in its slot (if_setobject) and colours its name and bars,
// as void-634's Anvil.kt does. smithing.dbtable gives each of 289's products
// its slot; the buttons below find the product by the slot and the bar.
//
// 2011's anvil adds crossbow bolts and limbs, nails of every metal, the iron
// spit, the bullseye lantern frame, the mithril grapple tip and pickaxes,
// which 289 does not make; their slots stay hidden until they are ported.

// 2011's buttons, Make All, X, 5 and 1 under each slot, where 289 had Make 1,
// 5 and 10 on each inv column (inv_button1-3).
// Dagger
[if_button,smithing_new:com_21] @smithing_anvil_button(smithing_new:com_18, ^smithing_make_all);
[if_button,smithing_new:com_22] @smithing_anvil_button(smithing_new:com_18, ^smithing_make_x);
[if_button,smithing_new:com_23] @smithing_anvil_button(smithing_new:com_18, 5);
[if_button,smithing_new:com_24] @smithing_anvil_button(smithing_new:com_18, 1);
